50; <bold>C</bold>, &#x000d7; 150; <bold>D</bold>, &#x000d7; 500; <bold>E</bold>, &#x000d7; 200; <bold>F</bold>, &#x000d7; 250.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="jpeg" xlink:href="92-6602245f1"/></fig><fig id="fig2"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>Box plot of VEGF cytoplasmic score stratified according to the WHO classification. Differences between groups were statistically significant (<italic>P</italic>=0.03).</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="gif" xlink:href="92-6602245f2"/></fig><fig id="fig3"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Box plot of HIF-1<italic>&#x003b1;</italic> cytoplasmic score stratified according to the WHO classification. Differences between groups were statistically significant (<italic>P</italic>=0.008).</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="gif" xlink:href="92-6602245f3"/></fig><fig id="fig4"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>Box plot of HIF-1<italic>&#x003b1;</italic> nuclear expression stratified according to the WHO classification. Differences between groups were statistically significant (<italic>P</italic>=0.001).</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="gif" xlink:href="92-6602245f4"/></fig><fig id="fig5"><label>Figure 5</label><caption><p>Immunohistochemical expression of CA9 and CD34 by WHO-stage 1 (<bold>A, B</bold>) and WHO-stage 4 (<bold>C, D</bold>) pancreatic endocrine tumours and by VHL cases (<bold>E, F</bold>). (<bold>A, C, E</bold>) CA9 is not detected in most well-differentiated PETs (<bold>A</bold>). Its expression is strong and membranous around areas of necrosis in WHO-stage 4 PETs (<bold>C</bold>) and cytoplasmic diffuse in VHL cases (<bold>E</bold>). (<bold>B, D, F</bold>) CD34&#x0002b; capillaries are numerous in WHO-stage 1 PETs (<bold>B</bold>) and scattered in WHO-stage 4 PETs (<bold>D</bold>). Microvascular density is very high in VHL cases (<bold>F</bold>). Immunoperoxidase and haematoxylin nuclear counterstaining; original magnifications: <bold>A</bold>, &#x000d7; 150; <bold>B</bold>, &#x000d7; 250; <bold>C</bold>, &#x000d7; 200; <bold>D</bold>, &#x000d7; 150; <bold>E</bold>, &#x000d7; 200; <bold>F</bold>, &#x000d7; 250.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="jpeg" xlink:href="92-6602245f5"/></fig><fig id="fig6"><label>Figure 6</label><caption><p>Box plot of CA9 membranous expression stratified according to the WHO classification. Differences between groups were statistically significant (<italic>P</italic>=0.0001).</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="gif" xlink:href="92-6602245f6"/></fig><fig id="fig7"><label>Figure 7</label><caption><p>Survival curves according to Kaplan&#x02013;Meier for 43 of the 45 patients of the study group according to CA9 membranous expression (thin line) or absence of expression (bold line); <italic>P</italic>=0.0004.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="gif" xlink:href="92-6602245f7"/></fig><fig id="fig8"><label>Figure 8</label><caption><p>Box plot of MVD recorded in hotspots stratified according to the WHO classification. Differences between groups were statistically significant (<italic>P</italic>=0.0001).</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="gif" xlink:href="92-6602245f8"/></fig><fig id="fig9"><label>Figure 9</label><caption><p>Survival curves according to Kaplan&#x02013;Meier for 43 of the 45 patients of the study group according to MVD &#x0003c;200&#x02009;mm<sup>&#x02212;2</sup> (thin line) or &#x0003e;200&#x02009;mm<sup>&#x02212;2</sup> (bold line); <italic>P</italic>=0.0001.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="gif" xlink:href="92-6602245f9"/></fig><table-wrap id="tbl1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Patients demographic